/-
Inst/Model/TablesData.lean: the numbers of the integer model's five lookup tables, as packed arrays.

Generated data, not meant to be read; unpacked in Inst/Model/TablesRef.lean. Each array holds blocks
of 1,024 entries; an entry has 13 bits (SILU + 4,095; SIGM / 16; Exp) or 14 bits (C + 4,096; S +
4,096); entry k of a block is at the bits from 13 k (or 14 k) on. SILU and SIGM: entry c + 2^14
belongs to the argument ι = c + 2^15, −2^14 ≤ c < 2^14. C and S: entry 64 i + ȷ (i: the position; ȷ:
the index of a pair of channels of a head: `Tables`, Inst/Model/Program.lean). The program that
generated the numbers is not part of this library.

Limits: no theorem says that the numbers are the rounded values of the real functions (SiLU,
sigmoid, exp, cos and sin: Inst/Model/Tables.lean).
-/
